    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nStunning penthouse apartment in one of Dublin's most sought-after coastal locations. With a magnificent roof garden set against a breathtaking backdrop of panoramic views stretching from Killiney Hill, sea views over Killiney Bay and out towards Bray Head. \n\nSet within a truly picture-postcard setting in the heart of Killiney Village, this two-bedroom penthouse offers a rare combination of generous accommodation across one level, a superb outdoor space and breathtaking views. A standout feature is the sizable private roof garden, which takes full advantage of its elevated position with a unique outlook over Killiney Hill Park and the beautiful sea views beyond. \n\nInternally, the accommodation is centred around a generous open-plan living and dining area, well-proportioned with ample space for a large dining table seating 10 to 12 guests. Three striking square picture windows frame far-reaching views across Dublin Bay and the skyline, an ever-changing outlook that brings the setting into the heart of the home. Floor-to-ceiling sliding doors open onto the private roof garden, where the outlook is unobstructed and private, taking in the full beauty of Killiney Hill.\n\nThe fitted kitchen is equipped with integrated appliances and a breakfast bar seating area ideal for casual dining. A useful utility room is positioned off the inner hallway. \n\nBedroom two is peacefully positioned to the rear of the property and benefits from an en-suite shower room. The primary bedroom is a generous double, fitted with wall-to-wall wardrobes and is opposite a well-appointed family bathroom, which completes the internal accommodation.\n\nOutside, the roof garden is one of the finest along the coast, generous in size and laid in Astro lawn, creating a low-maintenance outdoor space that flows directly from the living accommodation, making it feel like a natural extension of the home. Set on one level, the garden enjoys excellent sunshine throughout the day and is the ideal venue for outdoor dining and entertaining, while the elevated position captures some of the best views Killiney has to offer. \n\nThe location itself needs little introduction - situated on Killiney Hill Road in the heart of Killiney Village and just a short stroll from Killiney Hill, Killiney Beach and the DART it couldn't be more convenient. Fitzpatrick's Castle is also close by with its excellent leisure facilities. There is a regular bus service No. 59 into nearby Dalkey and Dun Laoghaire, offering you an excellent choice of amenities including restaurants, shopping facilities, schools and some of the town's most enjoyable walks."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nFront Door Landing: - \nA private landing with entrance door opening through to the accommodation.\n\nLiving/Dining Room: - \nA superb dual-aspect open-plan living/dining room with tiled flooring and impressive picture windows framing views down the slopes of Killiney Hill and out over the sea to Bray Head. The room is finished with a contemporary gas fireplace, central ceiling light, and a large section of floor-to-ceiling glazing with sliding doors opening onto the private roof garden with a stunning outlook over Killiney Hill Park and Killiney Bay. The dining is open plan of the living area and provides ample room for a large dining table comfortably seating 10 to 12 people.\n\nKitchen: - \nA galley style kitchen with tiled flooring, a range of wall and base-level storage cabinets, breakfast bar seating, and a picture window overlooking Killiney Hill. The kitchen includes a stainless-steel sink unit, provision for a fridge freezer, built-in oven, gas hob, extractor fan, recessed lighting, and dishwasher.\n\nInner Hallway: - \nWith book storage and a door through to the utility room.\n\nBedroom 1: - \nA spacious double bedroom with wall-to-wall fitted wardrobes and three picture windows to the rear.\n\nBathroom: - \nA well-appointed main bathroom with tiled flooring and partially tiled walls, comprising a full bath with shower attachment, wash hand basin, WC, and recessed lighting.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nA double bedroom with tiled flooring, recessed lighting, window, and door opening onto the rear.\n\nEn-Suite: - \nAn ensuite shower room with tiled walls and partially tiled floor, comprising a walk-in shower, wash hand basin, and WC.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Stunning penthouse apartment in the heart of Killiney Village </li><li> Private development of 4-residences </li><li> Accommodation laid out over one level </li><li> Elevated position with panoramic sea views </li><li> Vistas over Killiney Hill Park, Killiney Bay to Bray Head </li><li> Sizable private roof terrace enjoying excellent sunshine </li><li> Large open-plan living/dining room </li><li> Two bedrooms and two bathrooms </li><li> Excellent privacy and unobstructed outlook </li><li> Two car parking spaces </li><li> Resident vehicular gate via Talbot Lane</li><li> Short stroll to Killiney Hill, Killiney Beach and DART</li><li> Stroll to the Druids Chair Pub and Mister Magpie Coffee</ul>"
      },
